  "whatsNewTitle": "What's New",
  "whatsNewDescription": "The main changes in this release.",
  "whatsNewBadge": "NEW",
  "whatsNewSectionNew": "New",
  "whatsNewSectionImprovements": "Improvements",
  "whatsNewSectionFixes": "Fixes",
  "whatsNew020New1": "Managed Runtime installs and keeps PocketClaw's bundled tools up to date for you.",
  "whatsNew020New2": "Bundled developer tools: Git, GitHub CLI, curl, ripgrep, jq and SQLite.",
  "whatsNew020New3": "Support for PocketClaw's bundled Python 3.14 runtime.",
  "whatsNew020New4": "Secure GitHub sign-in, shared by the bundled Git and GitHub CLI.",
  "whatsNew020New5": "One-tap Telegram setup: PocketClaw creates your own bot, in the app or from the Dashboard in a browser. There is no token to copy, and only your own account can talk to it.",
  "whatsNew020New6": "A Status view on the Dashboard: active work, channels, the model in use and runtime resources.",
  "whatsNew020Improvement1": "More resilient providers: a failing request no longer ends the turn.",
  "whatsNew020Improvement2": "A more accurate Managed Runtime catalog.",
  "whatsNew020Improvement3": "A cleaner PocketClaw identity across the web interface and the default workspace.",
  "whatsNew020Improvement4": "A new app icon and a refreshed About screen, drawn from PocketClaw's Aperture design.",
  "whatsNew020Improvement5": "Assistant replies read more naturally, without a fixed sign-off at the end.",
  "whatsNew020Improvement6": "PocketClaw no longer asks for the Phone permission — nothing in the app used it.",
  "whatsNew020Improvement7": "Diagnostic logs are now kept privately inside the app instead of in your Downloads folder. Your workspace stays where it was.",
  "whatsNew020Improvement8": "A substantial upgrade to how PocketClaw keeps its state and runs its services, for steadier day-to-day reliability.",
  "whatsNew020Improvement9": "After this update, the Dashboard asks you to sign in once more.",
  "whatsNew020Improvement10": "After this update, the Web chat channel starts a new conversation.",
  "whatsNew020Improvement11": "After this update, it is worth checking your notification preferences once.",
  "whatsNew020Fix1": "The Gateway now recovers from a stale process record left behind by an earlier run.",
  "whatsNew020Fix2": "Channel lists with more than one entry are preserved correctly when settings are saved.",
